\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Five-fold detector-only SisFall context at the reported Youden operating points, $20{,}000$ standard-protocol windows/fold (prevalence $0.329$--$0.345$). E1 and retrained zoo are distinct checkpoint runs. Mean$\pm $sample std are recomputed from the supplied three-decimal fold F1 values; last-digit differences from separately supplied aggregate summaries can result from rounding. Neither run is the frozen main comparison or the separate $30{,}000$-window v2 evaluation. Scores describe tested implementations and training settings, not a universal architecture ranking.}}{1}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:backbone}{{S1}{1}{Five-fold detector-only SisFall context at the reported Youden operating points, $20{,}000$ standard-protocol windows/fold (prevalence $0.329$--$0.345$). E1 and retrained zoo are distinct checkpoint runs. Mean$\pm $sample std are recomputed from the supplied three-decimal fold F1 values; last-digit differences from separately supplied aggregate summaries can result from rounding. Neither run is the frozen main comparison or the separate $30{,}000$-window v2 evaluation. Scores describe tested implementations and training settings, not a universal architecture ranking}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces Multi-seed robustness on SisFall Fold\nobreakspace  {}0 ($n{=}1000$, Ollama/Mistral backend). Seeds redraw the stratified test slice as well as training randomness, so absolute values differ from the Fold\nobreakspace  {}0 row of the main-paper per-fold table (Table\nobreakspace  {}II, which uses the locked seed-42 slice); the quantity of interest is the across-seed spread, not the level.}}{1}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:seeds}{{S2}{1}{Multi-seed robustness on SisFall Fold~0 ($n{=}1000$, Ollama/Mistral backend). Seeds redraw the stratified test slice as well as training randomness, so absolute values differ from the Fold~0 row of the main-paper per-fold table (Table~II, which uses the locked seed-42 slice); the quantity of interest is the across-seed spread, not the level}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {S-III}Supplementary Results}{1}{section.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sup:results}{{S-III}{1}{Supplementary Results}{section.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces Sensor-perturbation robustness of primary-detector routing under the cost gate (SisFall, five-fold mean F1). Rotations apply a random rigid rotation of the sensor frame with the stated bound, emulating garment or mounting drift; resampling emulates a different device sampling rate. Degradation is graceful---the worst case, $\pm 15^\circ $, loses $0.014$ F1---so the ambiguous band is not an artefact of one exact sensor placement.}}{2}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:robustness}{{S3}{2}{Sensor-perturbation robustness of primary-detector routing under the cost gate (SisFall, five-fold mean F1). Rotations apply a random rigid rotation of the sensor frame with the stated bound, emulating garment or mounting drift; resampling emulates a different device sampling rate. Degradation is graceful---the worst case, $\pm 15^\circ $, loses $0.014$ F1---so the ambiguous band is not an artefact of one exact sensor placement}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces Archived pooled routing diagnostic without System\nobreakspace  {}2. The entries labelled min-cost and Q25 tie at reported cost $1015$, while Q25 has $23$ percentage points less deferral. Under these displayed objectives, min-cost is dominated; the source selection rule and the treatment of deferred-case errors must be distinguished from the production routing surrogate. These pooled points do not justify choosing deployment thresholds without held-out calibration and adjudicator evaluation.}}{2}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:pareto}{{S4}{2}{Archived pooled routing diagnostic without System~2. The entries labelled min-cost and Q25 tie at reported cost $1015$, while Q25 has $23$ percentage points less deferral. Under these displayed objectives, min-cost is dominated; the source selection rule and the treatment of deferred-case errors must be distinguished from the production routing surrogate. These pooled points do not justify choosing deployment thresholds without held-out calibration and adjudicator evaluation}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S5}{\ignorespaces Second-dataset evaluation on KFall, frozen primary detector versus full stack under the binary Fall/ADL protocol ($n{=}1000$/fold). This is not evidence of zero-shot transfer of SisFall-trained weights or formal non-inferiority. Fold\nobreakspace  {}1 regresses; Fold\nobreakspace  {}4 has the largest displayed F1 gain. Deltas below are computed from the displayed rounded values. Fold\nobreakspace  {}4 primary row is consistent with its confusion counts (TP${=}473$, TN${=}508$, FP${=}9$, FN${=}10$; $483$ falls, not $\approx $499 as in other folds): F1 $0.980$, recall $0.979$, cost $109$.}}{3}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:kfallperfold}{{S5}{3}{Second-dataset evaluation on KFall, frozen primary detector versus full stack under the binary Fall/ADL protocol ($n{=}1000$/fold). This is not evidence of zero-shot transfer of SisFall-trained weights or formal non-inferiority. Fold~1 regresses; Fold~4 has the largest displayed F1 gain. Deltas below are computed from the displayed rounded values. Fold~4 primary row is consistent with its confusion counts (TP${=}473$, TN${=}508$, FP${=}9$, FN${=}10$; $483$ falls, not $\approx $499 as in other folds): F1 $0.980$, recall $0.979$, cost $109$}{table.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S6}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity to the clinical cost ratio $\beta =c_{\mathrm  {FN}}/c_{\mathrm  {FP}}$ (SisFall, five-fold mean cost per $1000$ windows, $\mathcal  {R}_\beta =\beta \cdot \mathrm  {FN}+\mathrm  {FP}$). The advantage of the stack is monotone in $\beta $: the more a deployment penalises missed falls relative to nuisance alarms, the larger the absolute saving. $\tau ^\ast =1/(\beta {+}1)$ is the corresponding hard-decision Bayes threshold\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:tau_star}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}. The $\beta {=}10$ row is the paper's primary setting.}}{3}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:betacost}{{S6}{3}{Sensitivity to the clinical cost ratio $\beta =c_{\mathrm {FN}}/c_{\mathrm {FP}}$ (SisFall, five-fold mean cost per $1000$ windows, $\mathcal {R}_\beta =\beta \cdot \mathrm {FN}+\mathrm {FP}$). The advantage of the stack is monotone in $\beta $: the more a deployment penalises missed falls relative to nuisance alarms, the larger the absolute saving. $\tau ^\ast =1/(\beta {+}1)$ is the corresponding hard-decision Bayes threshold~\eqref {eq:tau_star}. The $\beta {=}10$ row is the paper's primary setting}{table.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S7}{\ignorespaces Rationale grounding. $\mathcal  {G}_{\mathrm  {faith}}$ is the fraction of rationales that mention at least one evidence field present in $\Sigma (\mathbf  {x})$. It is a prompt-compliance check, not a measure of reasoning faithfulness or correctness: a rationale can cite a field and still reach the wrong conclusion. \emph  {Graded cost} scores the four-level simulated action rather than the binary label. Contrastive critique with frozen labels raises $\mathcal  {G}_{\mathrm  {faith}}$ ($0.436{\rightarrow }0.843$) and lowers graded action cost by $45\%$.}}{3}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:grounding}{{S7}{3}{Rationale grounding. $\mathcal {G}_{\mathrm {faith}}$ is the fraction of rationales that mention at least one evidence field present in $\Sigma (\mathbf {x})$. It is a prompt-compliance check, not a measure of reasoning faithfulness or correctness: a rationale can cite a field and still reach the wrong conclusion. \emph {Graded cost} scores the four-level simulated action rather than the binary label. Contrastive critique with frozen labels raises $\mathcal {G}_{\mathrm {faith}}$ ($0.436{\rightarrow }0.843$) and lowers graded action cost by $45\%$}{table.7}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S8}{\ignorespaces System\nobreakspace  {}2 duty cycle by evaluation protocol. The $1000$-window SisFall rate comes from the separate timing run, not the primary classification counts. SisFall protocols are stratified and D18/D19 enriched: these rates constrain feasibility but are neither free-living estimates nor guaranteed upper bounds. Distribution shift can change escalation in either direction. Binary KFall invokes deliberation on roughly one window in ninety under its own protocol.}}{3}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:escalation}{{S8}{3}{System~2 duty cycle by evaluation protocol. The $1000$-window SisFall rate comes from the separate timing run, not the primary classification counts. SisFall protocols are stratified and D18/D19 enriched: these rates constrain feasibility but are neither free-living estimates nor guaranteed upper bounds. Distribution shift can change escalation in either direction. Binary KFall invokes deliberation on roughly one window in ninety under its own protocol}{table.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S9}{\ignorespaces Processing latency from the separate Ollama/Mistral agentic timing run (SisFall, $n{=}1000$/fold; GPU evaluation, not wearable hardware). The primary detector is evaluated for every window; the escalated path is dominated by local LLM decoding. Mean stack is the measured per-window average. Fold\nobreakspace  {}2 has the slowest escalated path ($22.85$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}s), not the highest duty cycle (its rate is $0.460$, versus $0.546$ on Fold\nobreakspace  {}4). Window acquisition, queueing and clinical response time are not established by these measurements.}}{3}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:latency}{{S9}{3}{Processing latency from the separate Ollama/Mistral agentic timing run (SisFall, $n{=}1000$/fold; GPU evaluation, not wearable hardware). The primary detector is evaluated for every window; the escalated path is dominated by local LLM decoding. Mean stack is the measured per-window average. Fold~2 has the slowest escalated path ($22.85$\,s), not the highest duty cycle (its rate is $0.460$, versus $0.546$ on Fold~4). Window acquisition, queueing and clinical response time are not established by these measurements}{table.9}{}}
